# Next.js 15 App Router Patterns

## Route Structure
```
src/app/
  layout.tsx              # Root layout (Clerk + Convex providers)
  (public)/
    page.tsx              # Public homepage
    events/page.tsx
    directory/page.tsx
    blog/[slug]/page.tsx
  admin/
    layout.tsx            # Admin layout (sidebar, auth guard)
    page.tsx              # Admin dashboard
    calendars/page.tsx
    contacts/page.tsx
    contacts/[id]/page.tsx
    purchases/page.tsx
    purchases/new/page.tsx
    billing/page.tsx
  portal/
    layout.tsx            # Portal layout (client auth guard)
    page.tsx
  auth/
    login/[[...login]]/page.tsx
    register/[[...register]]/page.tsx
```

## Component Conventions
- Page components: server components by default, `"use client"` only when needed
- Interactive components (forms, tables, dialogs): always `"use client"`
- Convex hooks (`useQuery`, `useMutation`) require `"use client"`
- Prefer composition: page fetches data, passes to client components

## Layout Pattern
```tsx
// src/app/admin/layout.tsx
import { AdminSidebar } from "@/components/admin/sidebar";
import { AdminHeader } from "@/components/admin/header";

export default function AdminLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <div className="flex h-screen">
      <AdminSidebar />
      <div className="flex-1 flex flex-col">
        <AdminHeader />
        <main className="flex-1 overflow-auto p-6">{children}</main>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Providers Setup (Root Layout)
```tsx
// src/app/layout.tsx
<ClerkProvider>
  <ConvexProviderWithClerk client={convex} useAuth={useAuth}>
    {children}
  </ConvexProviderWithClerk>
</ClerkProvider>
```

## Middleware
- Clerk middleware protects `/admin/*` and `/portal/*`
- Public routes (`/`, `/events`, `/directory`, `/blog`, `/coupons`, `/videos`) are unprotected
- Auth routes (`/auth/*`) are always accessible

## Import Aliases
- `@/` maps to `src/`
- `@/components/ui` for shadcn components
- `@/lib` for utilities, types, validators
- `@/hooks` for custom hooks
